      "side": 1,
      "message": "Incidentally, EthernetNetworkFactory#getAvailableInterfaces() (called from EthernetTracker#unicastInterfaceStateChange, the thing that calls you back after registering an interface state listener) sorts interfaces by name, so testtap%d callbacks always arrive after callbacks for eth%d. However, on V, the default configuration starts including usb%d ethernet interfaces (see https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Connectivity/service-t/src/com/android/server/ethernet/EthernetTracker.java;l\u003d247;drc\u003ddbbada4d7bdc48f3c2ec9981b3716662a5a2d5f8). Note that any device could have declared this in their config overlay even before V. So this could technically still break if a usb%d interface were present (when calling `listener.expectCallback(iface, STATE_LINK_DOWN, ROLE_CLIENT)`)\n\nMaybe you want to add an additional eventuallyExpect() call after the first disableInterface() and add another\n```\n        disableInterface(iface).expectResult(iface.name)\n        listener.expectCallback(iface, STATE_LINK_DOWN, ROLE_CLIENT)\n```\nblock at the end of the test.",
